    {
      "id": "pF6cuplBw3HannLz4l0EA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2459.4148333761673,
      "y": -4483.121189480089,
      "width": 667.0136682116173,
      "height": 282.9955136557746,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#fcc2d7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1177089888,
      "version": 695,
      "versionNonce": 1351349920,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772391950386,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Orchestrator ↔ STT (The Ear): The Orchestrator streams raw audio from the call\nto the STT. The STT sends back \"interim transcripts\" (the AI sees the words as\nthe user is still speaking them).\n\nOrchestrator ↔ MIND (The LLM): Once a \"turn\" is detected, the text is sent to\nthe LLM. In a premium setup, the LLM starts streaming the response tokens back\nimmediately.\n\nOrchestrator ↔ TTS (The Mouth): The Orchestrator feeds those text tokens into\nthe TTS. The TTS starts generating audio for the first half of the sentence\nwhile the LLM is still thinking of the second half.\n\nOrchestrator ↔ Call Engine: This is the bridge to the real world. The\nOrchestrator sends the final synthesized audio to the Call Engine (Twilio/Vapi)\nto be played into the student's ear.",
      "fontSize": 15.09309406164131,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Orchestrator ↔ STT (The Ear): The Orchestrator streams raw audio from the call to the STT. The STT sends back \"interim transcripts\" (the AI sees the words as the user is still speaking them).\n\nOrchestrator ↔ MIND (The LLM): Once a \"turn\" is detected, the text is sent to the LLM. In a premium setup, the LLM starts streaming the response tokens back immediately.\n\nOrchestrator ↔ TTS (The Mouth): The Orchestrator feeds those text tokens into the TTS. The TTS starts generating audio for the first half of the sentence while the LLM is still thinking of the second half.\n\nOrchestrator ↔ Call Engine: This is the bridge to the real world. The Orchestrator sends the final synthesized audio to the Call Engine (Twilio/Vapi) to be played into the student's ear.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lIT5Rkt8svq7RUCZzXw-Q",
      "type": "arrow",
      "x": -1589.3739385869792,
      "y": -4780.627636492989,
      "width": 178.24081697113002,
      "height": 1.8294435380985306,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
